      "message": "Just use __hw_clock_source_read(), that\u0027ll give you a 32-bit value.\n\nThe snippet below should do the right thing, even if the value overflows:\n\n  uint32_t start \u003d __hw_clock_source_read();\n\n  if ((__hw_clock_source_read() - start) \u003e LPC_HOST_TRANSACTION_TIMEOUT_US) {\n     // timeout!\n  }",
